  "description": "Project IGFPROJECT1 will be processed under the supervision of John\u202fDoe (HPC username: jdoe_hpc; local username: jdoe; email: jdoe@example.com). The sample to be sequenced is identified as IGFSAMPLE1 with the submitter\u2011provided ID SUB\u2011001. Barcode verification is enabled (ON) and the organism is Homo sapiens (taxon ID 9606), referenced by the genome build HG38. The donor is anonymized as DONOR123, described as a healthy male (sex: MALE) of 30\u202fY age, belonging to a European population, with the phenotype \u201chealthy\u201d, treatment \u201cnone\u201d, and trait \u201cheight\u201d. The biomaterial type is PRIMARY_TISSUE, specifically a skin fibroblast (cell type: fibroblast; tissue type: skin). No cell line information is provided for this sample.\n\nThe library has been assigned the identifier IGFLIB001 and originates from a GENOMIC source, employing a Whole\u2011Genome Sequencing (WGS) strategy, with the experiment type also set to WGS. Library layout is PAIRED, and barcode removal is turned ON. The mean fragment length distribution is 350\u202fbp (SD\u202f20\u202fbp) with an insert length of 370\u202fbp. Adapter sequences used are AGATCGGAAGAGCACACGTCTGAACTCCAGTCAC (adapter\u202f1) and AGATCGGAAGAGCGTCGTGTAGGGAAAGAGTGT (adapter\u202f2). Expected output is 50\u202f000\u202f000 reads across 2 lanes.",
